::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-printer, dependencies: list(tomet-ast, tomet-ast-parser, tomet-config, tomet-field-utils, tomet-formatter, tomet-markdown, tomet-semantics, tomet-span, tomet-style, tomet-tree), dependents: list(tomet, tomet-cli, tomet-convert-standalone, tomet-html, tomet-markdown, tomet-pandoc, tomet-spec, tomet-tests, tomet-typst, tomet-workspace)}

=[tomet-printer]

Serializes a `tomet_ast::Document` back to `.tmt` source text
(no span info required, unlike `tomet-formatter`, which
re-formats existing `.tmt` text losslessly using spans -- this crate
is for documents that never had `.tmt` source to begin with, e.g.
ones built from Markdown or edited purely at the AST level). Uses
`tomet_config::PrinterConfig` (see that crate for config
loading/discovery) to drive formatting choices: meta format
(yaml/json/toml), link-key spacing, callout/list style, via
`tomet-style`'s single-node renderers. Also owns `::meta` id
auto-generation (`ensure_document_id_with_config`, which mutates the
AST directly), built on the pure generate/validate/convert helpers
in `tomet-field-utils`.

==[Module block]

Rendering blocks, sections, headings, and lists.

==[Module element]

Rendering elements, values, args, and connects.

===[Functions]

====[fn render_element]

Render an [`Element`] AST node into Tomet syntax:
`<sigil><name>(args)[content]{value}`.

====[fn render_bare]

Render a [`Bare`] entry into Tomet syntax: `(args)[content]{value}#(id)`,
with no head.

====[fn render_hole]

Render a [`Hole`] AST node into Tomet syntax:
`<?matcher(args){value}>[content]`.

The head, the matcher and the `(args)` and `{value}` groups, is inside the box and
the `[content]` follows its `>`, however `args` and `content` are ordered for an element.

====[fn render_declaration]

Render a [`Declaration`] AST node into Tomet syntax:
`::name(args)[content]{value}#(id)`.

==[Module id]

ID generation and rendering helpers.

===[Functions]

====[fn ensure_document_id_with_config]

Ensures that a document has an `::id(...)` declaration if configured to do so.

The generation is configured by the vault's `id` meta field (`type`, `force`, `overwrite`, ...).
A new declaration goes after the leading `::version` / `::kind`, so the preamble reads
`::kind`, `::id`, `::meta`.

==[Module inline]

Rendering inline content and block-permitted content runs.

==[Functions]

===[fn document_to_tm]

Serialize a [`Document`] AST into Tomet (`.tmt`) source string using document-level config or defaults.

===[fn hole_to_tm]

A [`tomet_ast::Hole`] as the box it was written as, `<?matcher(args){value}>[content]`,
with the document-independent default configuration.

For a reader that has no rendering of a hole and shows it as it was written, the way an
interpolation nobody evaluated is shown (`tomet-convert-*`).

